cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Infiniteworlds in academic work, research, or derivative projects, please cite it as below."
title: "Infiniteworlds: A Voice-Interactive, Multi-Agent LLM-Driven 3D World Engine"
abstract: >-
  Infiniteworlds is an open-source, never-ending storytelling engine that
  generates infinitely morphing 3D worlds from natural-language conversation.
  It combines a multi-agent LLM architecture (World GM, Companion, Task
  Generator) routed through a local provider-aggregator proxy, real-time
  voice I/O via Whisper and ElevenLabs Conversational AI, procedural
  Babylon.js terrain across five scale tiers (cosmic to nano), and a
  persistent "legacy echo" memory layer that lets deleted worlds bleed
  fragments into future ones.
